  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We are given the unit rate of $$2$ per ounce (dollars per ounce). To find how many ounces of specialty cheese he can buy for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in ounces per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n2\\,\\text{dollars per ounce}\\,\\to \\,1÷2=0.5\\,\\text{ounces per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.5$ ounces per dollar. Therefore, Rohan can buy $0.5$ ounces of specialty cheese for $1$ dollar.",
